```python
import json

input_str = """
{
    "output_list": [
        {
            "function_name": "<function_name>",
            "code": "<code>",
            "vulnerability": "<short_vulnera_desc>",
            "reason": "<reason>"
        }
    ]
}
"""

# Load the input JSON
input_json = json.loads(input_str)

# Extract the first dictionary in output_list and save it as output
output = input_json["output_list"][0]

# Format the output into the desired format
output = {
    "output_list": [
        output
    ]
}

# Convert the output back to a JSON string
output_str = json.dumps(output, indent=4)

# Print the output
print(output_str)
```

This script will load the input JSON, extract the first dictionary in `output_list`, and format it into the desired output format. The final output JSON string will be printed to the console. Replace `<function_name>`, `<code>`, `<short_vulnera_desc>`, and `<reason>` with the actual values you want to include in the output JSON.